51
00:02:53.683 --> 00:02:56.101
Grammar focus: used to / would.

52
00:02:56.401 --> 00:02:59.689
Use used to for past habits and states that are no longer true.

53
00:02:59.989 --> 00:03:03.359
Would can also describe past habits, but not states.

54
00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:09.132
For example: We used to walk to school. Every evening, my mother would check my homework.

55
00:03:09.432 --> 00:03:12.372
The negative is didn't use to, and the question is Did you use to ...?

56
00:03:13.383 --> 00:03:15.989
Now read and listen. From Chalk to Chat.

57
00:03:16.289 --> 00:03:19.566
Fifty years ago, Cambodian classrooms looked very different.

58
00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:24.452
Students used to share books and write on small slates.

59
00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:29.851
Teachers would ask questions, and the whole class would repeat the answers.

60
00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:34.949
Today, many students take online courses and learn from videos.

61
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.502
Technology has changed how we learn, but good teachers are still essential.

